From 5278342497729e1d8eb011c35a0cb1510122422f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanbang <hanbang@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:20:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Libretro: add Beetle WonderSwan Dual (two WonderSwans on
 one link cable)

dual/libretro_dual.c is a new libretro frontend that runs two copies of
this core, built twice with every external name prefixed (wsA_, wsB_;
dual/build_dual.sh generates the prefix headers from the plain build),
and steps them line by line, handing finished serial bytes to the other
console after both ran the line. Port 0 drives the 1P console, port 1
the 2P console; wswan_dual_screen picks whose picture and sound are
output, wswan_dual_link=off runs the 1P console alone. Options that must
match between netplay peers are fixed by the wrapper. Savestates hold
both consoles; the 2P save is <save dir>/<rom>.p2.sav (copied from the
1P save when missing), written by the host only.

---
 dual/build_dual.sh   |   64 +++
 dual/exports_mac.txt |    1 +
 dual/libretro_dual.c | 1116 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dual/link_dual.T     |    4 +
